# ${RECIPE_NAME}

Customer-built **${ACCEL_KEY}** universal workbench for OpenShift AI / ODH.

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Stack | ${STACK} |
| Collections | ${COLLECTIONS} |
| Constraints | `constraints.txt` (ABI ceiling; latest *within* range) |
| Product base | ${PRODUCT} (${INDEX_KIND} index) |
| Base image | `${BASE_IMAGE}` |
| Python index | `${INDEX_URL}` |
| Platform | `${PLATFORM}` |
| Image | `${IMAGE_REF}` |

**One digest** for interactive **Jupyter** and **Elyra pipeline runtime**
([RHAIENG-7241](https://redhat.atlassian.net/browse/RHAIENG-7241) §1).

| Mode | How it starts |
|------|----------------|
| Workbench | Default `ENTRYPOINT` → `start-notebook.sh` (JupyterLab) |
| Runtime (cluster) | Elyra/KFP sets `command: [sh, -c]` (replaces ENTRYPOINT) and runs the bootstrapper |
| Runtime (local probe) | `entrypoint.sh runtime …` or `WORKBENCH_MODE=runtime` |

ImageStream labels advertise both `opendatahub.io/notebook-image` and
`opendatahub.io/runtime-image` for the same tag.

## Layout

```text
Containerfile
pyproject.toml             # Jupyter + Elyra runtime deps (unpinned)
requirements.txt
build-args/${CONF_NAME}
collections/               # curated use-case package sets (RHAIENG-7241 §3)
bin/entrypoint.sh
bin/validate-universal.sh
bin/utils/bootstrapper.py
bin/utils/requirements-elyra.txt   # blank (skip Elyra curl of full list)
imagestream.yaml           # dual notebook + runtime labels
```

Sibling of `src/`. Do not put generated images inside `src/`.

## Package collections

If `collections/` contains TrustyAI or LLM Compressor metadata, those packages were
merged into `pyproject.toml` / `requirements.txt` from the RH (or PyPI) index —
not from a specialized OOTB image. **Do not mix TrustyAI with PyTorch/LLM Compressor
in the same `site-packages`** (numpy/pandas ABI). Use two images or an isolated venv.

```bash
make collections                 # discover available collections in src/
make validate RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME}   # import-check after build
make validate-universal RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME}  # §1 dual-mode checks
```

## Prerequisites

1. **Entitlements (AIPCC/RHEL only)** — before `make build`, register once and mount
   certs via podman `mounts.conf`. See
   [custom-workbenches/README.md](../README.md) § Recommended workflow and
   [docs/subscribed-builds.md](../../docs/subscribed-builds.md).
2. `podman` (or Docker), network to the base registry and `${INDEX_URL}`
3. Cluster: OpenShift AI / ODH, GPU Operator when using CUDA/ROCm, Quay pull secret

ODH (CentOS Stream) bases do not need RHSM entitlements.

## Build, push, validate

From `custom-workbenches/`:

```bash
make build RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME} PUSH_IMAGES=no
make validate-universal RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME}
make validate RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME}
make push RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME}
make build RECIPE=${RECIPE_NAME} PLATFORM=linux/arm64
```

## Import (same digest, two roles)

1. Dashboard → **Settings → Workbench images → Import** → `${IMAGE_REF}`
2. Apply `imagestream.yaml` (or import again as a **pipeline runtime**) so Elyra
   lists the **same digest** under runtime images
3. Launch a workbench from that image; in Elyra, select the same image as the
   node runtime and run a one-node pipeline

## Support boundary

Customer-built. Not a Red Hat OOTB workbench. You own CVEs, validation, and mirroring.

